Sidon k=8      553.2     324      156         49.6   11.146   9.878
AP7 d=1       1494.4     593      488        155.2    9.627   8.211

STATEMENT (E_3):  E_3 = RES_33/(s^{2(k-3)} c_3) is the ORDER-3 ADDITIVE ENERGY -- the
count of matched balanced 3-term relations sum w_a E_a = sum w'_b E_b (!=0), weighted by
the tent kernel.  Dominant carrier = the (1,1,-2) form E_i+E_j-2E_l, L^2 mass sum Q(nu)^2
(the triple analog of R2=sum_d r_d^2); E_3 ~ 9-10x its raw offdiagonal (other order-3
forms + harmonics).  NOTE E_2 itself is ~1.6x R2/2 (a>=2 harmonics + doublings), so the
naive energies are LEADING terms, not exact.

!! PER-LEVEL DIVERGENCE (honest caveat) !!  For the CLUSTERED block k=11 the per-level
   E_p GROW (E_3=22k,E_4=608k,E_5=8M): the series sum_j E_j c_j s^{2(k-j)} does NOT
   converge term-by-term; Var survives only by full coherent cancellation across ALL
   levels.  So brick(B) Var<=c*R2 CANNOT be proven by bounding E_3 alone.  This is the
   real form of kps-S82's 'non-perturbative': the DAMPED/coherent object converges
   (opus-S152) but the per-level RESONANCE series is asymptotic/divergent for clustered
   sets.  The block is exactly brick(A)'s EXCLUDED case (diam 10<16).

